Spec: Context

Purpose:
  Be the process-wide reconcile context of the crate: remember which one of the four package
    payloads — @JukeBox, @ServiceInstance, @TenantInstance, @SystemInstance, or the initial
    @VynilContext::None — the current work unit acts as, and turn that slot into the material
    applied objects need through @get_owner_ns, @get_owner and @get_labels; carry the cluster
    write identity (@get_client_name, @get_short_name, @get_reporter) and the @kube::Client
    suppliers @get_client and @get_client_async; @wire_core_k8s injects the accessors into
    `vynil-core` so generic apply paths label and own objects through the same context.

Owns:
  ./context.rs

References:
  ./tools.sdd, ./instancesystem.sdd — approved calibration references.

Must:
  The whole module shares one private @CONTEXT: a @std::sync::LazyLock over a
    @tokio::sync::RwLock<@VynilContext> initialized to @VynilContext::None; it is not `pub`,
    so @set_tenant, @set_service, @set_system, @set_box, @get_owner_ns, @get_owner and
    @get_labels are its only reaches and the stored value is global to the process for its
    lifetime with no reset or full-read surface.
  @VynilContext is a @pub enum deriving only @Debug and carrying exactly
    @VynilContext::JukeBox,
    @VynilContext::ServiceInstance, @VynilContext::TenantInstance,
    @VynilContext::SystemInstance and the unit variant @VynilContext::None.
  Every sync entry crosses the async state with @tokio::task::block_in_place wrapping
    @tokio::runtime::Handle::current().block_on, so the whole module's usability contract is
    "called on a live tokio multi-thread runtime"; the panic cases are frozen in Raises.
  @set_tenant, @set_service, @set_system and @set_box take the write lock and store their
    variant as the entire context: the previous value is dropped outright, from any variant
    and of any kind, so a later set always replaces an earlier one with no merge, version
    check or kind-transition guard.
  @get_owner_ns maps the stored variant one-to-one: the three instance variants return
    @Some of `metadata.namespace` cloned through @unwrap_or_default — an instance without a
    namespace yields @Some of an empty string, not @None — while @VynilContext::JukeBox and
    @VynilContext::None return @None.
  @get_owner returns @None only for @VynilContext::None; payload variants return a JSON
    object with exactly the keys `apiVersion` (literal `vynil.solidite.fr/v1`), `kind` (the
    payload kind string `TenantInstance`, `ServiceInstance`, `SystemInstance` or `JukeBox`),
    `name` and `uid` from `metadata` with an absent field serialized as `""`, and hard-coded
    `blockOwnerDeletion: true` plus `controller: true` — a JukeBox context therefore yields a
    JukeBox owner reference even though @get_owner_ns refuses one.
  @get_labels returns @None only for @VynilContext::None; every payload variant yields a
    label object carrying `app.kubernetes.io/managed-by` (literal `vynil`) and
    `app.kubernetes.io/instance` (from `metadata.name`, `""` when absent); the three instance
    variants add `app.kubernetes.io/name` from `spec.package`,
    `vynil.solidite.fr/owner-namespace` from `metadata.namespace` and
    `vynil.solidite.fr/owner-category` from `spec.category` (absent metadata fields become
    `""`); `vynil.solidite.fr/owner-type` distinguishes the variants as `tenant`, `system`,
    `service` or `jukebox`; the @VynilContext::JukeBox object carries only the three keys
    `app.kubernetes.io/managed-by`, `app.kubernetes.io/instance` and
    `vynil.solidite.fr/owner-type`.
  The @VynilContext::TenantInstance branch of @get_labels performs in-cluster I/O while
    holding the @CONTEXT read guard: it clones the @TenantInstance and calls
    @rhai_get_tenant_name, whose wrapper does a nested @tokio::task::block_in_place plus
    block_on over @TenantInstance::get_tenant_name — that path builds a fresh client via
    @get_client_async and reads the instance namespace metadata; the
    `vynil.solidite.fr/tenant` label value is the namespace value of the label key named by
    the `TENANT_LABEL` environment variable (default `vynil.solidite.fr/tenant`) or the
    instance namespace when the label is absent, and any failure — instance without a
    namespace, API unreachable — is swallowed to `""` with no propagation or log.
  Name identity derives from the executable: @get_prog_name (private) extracts
    @std::env::current_exe's file name through @to_str and yields @None on any failure;
    @get_client_name maps `agent` to `agent.vynil.solidite.fr`, `operator` to
    `controller.vynil.solidite.fr`, and every other file name or failure to
    `vynil.solidite.fr`.
  @get_short_name splits @get_client_name on `.` and returns `{second}-{first}` only when the
    split has more than three parts, `vynil` otherwise; the reachable results on this code
    are `vynil-agent` for the agent binary, `vynil-controller` for the operator binary and
    `vynil` for every other executable or failure, and a three-part client name can never
    shorten.
  @init_k8s is an empty `pub const fn` — calling it changes no state and only keeps its call
    sites compiling.
  @get_client and @get_client_async build a fresh @kube::Client::try_default on every call
    with no caching of any kind in this file; all discovery is delegated to
    @kube::Config::infer on the locked kube-client `3.1.0` build, which loads the kubeconfig
    from the `KUBECONFIG` environment variable or `~/.kube/config` first and falls back to
    the in-cluster configuration (the `KUBERNETES_SERVICE_HOST` and `KUBERNETES_SERVICE_PORT`
    environment variables plus the service-account token files) only when that kubeconfig
    load fails; the file itself contains no kubeconfig parsing, no in-cluster override and no
    in-cluster test fake.
  On client-build failure both suppliers @panic! with the message
    `cannot create the Kubernetes client: {e}` interpolating the @kube::Error Display, which
    for an unresolvable configuration carries the combined kubeconfig and in-cluster
    inference errors.
  @get_reporter stamps a @kube::runtime::events::Reporter with `controller` set to
    @get_short_name() and `instance` set to the `POD_NAME` environment variable re-read per
    call, literal `unknown` when unset.
  @wire_core_k8s registers exactly five hooks — @vynil_core::k8s::set_get_client(@get_client),
    @vynil_core::set_client_name(@get_client_name),
    @vynil_core::k8s::set_get_labels(@get_labels), @vynil_core::k8s::set_get_owner(@get_owner)
    and @vynil_core::k8s::set_get_owner_ns(@get_owner_ns) — each stored on the core side in a
    @std::sync::OnceLock through @set().ok(), so the first registration per hook sticks and
    any re-registration is silently ignored; @vynil_core::k8s::context_is_wired reports true
    only once all five are present, and the core lazy client reads the client hook with an
    @expect on first use, so wiring must precede the first core k8s call of the process.

Depends on:
  @crate::@JukeBox, @crate::@ServiceInstance, @crate::@SystemInstance, @crate::@TenantInstance
    — ./jukebox.rs, ./instanceservice.rs, ./instancesystem.rs, ./instancetenant.rs: payload
    `metadata` and `spec` fields and, on the tenant label path,
    @crate::TenantInstance::rhai_get_tenant_name → @crate::TenantInstance::get_tenant_name,
    which re-enters this module through @get_client_async — a real in-crate cycle between the
    context and the instance models.
  @kube::client::Client and @kube::runtime::events::Reporter — kube `3.1.0` locked in
    `/Cargo.lock` on workspace features `runtime`, `client`, `derive` from `/Cargo.toml`;
    @Client::try_default plus @kube::Config::infer perform every step of client construction
    and kubeconfig/in-cluster discovery.
  @tokio::sync::RwLock, @tokio::task::block_in_place, @tokio::runtime::Handle — tokio
    `1.48.0` requested in `/Cargo.toml`, `1.52.3` locked in `/Cargo.lock`; the panic texts in
    Raises are owned by that build, whose @block_in_place passes a plain thread through and
    refuses non-multi-thread scheduler contexts.
  `vynil-core` `0.7.7` locked in `/Cargo.lock` with feature `k8s` — the five @std::sync::OnceLock
    injection hooks @wire_core_k8s registers into.
  @serde_json — the @serde_json::Value carrier of the owner and label objects.
  @std::env — @std::env::current_exe for the binary identity and @std::env::var for
    `POD_NAME`.

Exposes:
  @VynilContext — @pub enum, @Debug the only derive, with variants @VynilContext::JukeBox(@JukeBox),
    @VynilContext::ServiceInstance(@ServiceInstance),
    @VynilContext::TenantInstance(@TenantInstance), @VynilContext::SystemInstance(@SystemInstance)
    and @VynilContext::None.
  @set_tenant — @pub fn @set_tenant(@i: @TenantInstance): installs the tenant variant.
  @set_service — @pub fn @set_service(@i: @ServiceInstance): installs the service variant.
  @set_system — @pub fn @set_system(@i: @SystemInstance): installs the system variant.
  @set_box — @pub fn @set_box(@jb: @JukeBox): installs the JukeBox variant.
  @get_owner_ns — @must_use @pub fn @get_owner_ns() -> @Option<@String>: owner namespace of
    an instance variant, empty string when the field is absent, @None for JukeBox and @None.
  @get_owner — @must_use @pub fn @get_owner() -> @Option<@serde_json::Value>: owner
    reference object for any payload variant, @None for @VynilContext::None.
  @get_labels — @must_use @pub fn @get_labels() -> @Option<@serde_json::Value>: label object
    for any payload variant, @None for @VynilContext::None; the tenant branch additionally
    performs a cluster namespace read with failures flattened to `""` (see Must).
  @get_client_name — @must_use @pub fn @get_client_name() -> @String, re-exported at the
    crate root by `./lib.rs`.
  @get_short_name — @must_use @pub fn @get_short_name() -> @String: `vynil-agent`,
    `vynil-controller` or `vynil`.
  @init_k8s — @pub const fn @init_k8s(): observable no-op.
  @get_client — @must_use @pub fn @get_client() -> @kube::Client: blocking client supplier
    requiring a multi-thread runtime, panics per Raises.
  @get_client_async — @pub async fn @get_client_async() -> @kube::Client: async twin of
    @get_client with the same per-call construction and panic contract, and no
    @must_use marker.
  @get_reporter — @must_use @pub fn @get_reporter() -> @kube::runtime::events::Reporter.
  @wire_core_k8s — @pub fn @wire_core_k8s(): first-wins registration of the five
    `vynil-core` hooks; idempotent by OnceLock design.

Accepts:
  The four setters each accept one owned payload by value — @JukeBox, @ServiceInstance,
    @TenantInstance or @SystemInstance — with no validation, deduplication or rejection of any
    kind: any instance value replaces the stored context unconditionally.
  @get_owner_ns, @get_owner, @get_labels, @get_client_name, @get_short_name, @get_reporter,
    @get_client, @init_k8s and @wire_core_k8s take no arguments; the sync ones among them
    carry as implicit precondition a live tokio multi-thread runtime (see Raises), and
    @get_labels on the tenant variant requires a reachable API server for a non-empty tenant
    label.
  @get_client and @get_client_async accept no configuration argument of any kind — endpoint,
    context and credentials all arrive from the process environment through
    @kube::Config::infer.

Returns:
  @set_tenant, @set_service, @set_system, @set_box, @init_k8s and @wire_core_k8s return `()`;
    state change is the only observable output.
  @get_owner_ns returns @Some(@String) for the three instance variants — the raw namespace or
    the empty string — and @None for JukeBox and @None contexts.
  @get_owner and @get_labels return the owner/label @serde_json::Value objects shaped in
    Must, or @None for @VynilContext::None.
  @get_client_name returns one of `agent.vynil.solidite.fr`, `controller.vynil.solidite.fr`
    or `vynil.solidite.fr`; @get_short_name returns one of `vynil-agent`, `vynil-controller`
    or `vynil`.
  @get_client and @get_client_async return a freshly constructed @kube::Client — a usable
    client is returned without probing the API server — or never return at all (panic).
  @get_reporter returns a @kube::runtime::events::Reporter with `controller` and `instance`
    populated as described in Must.

Raises:
  Every synchronous entry point that touches @CONTEXT and @get_client panics outside any
    tokio runtime before reading or writing state: @tokio::task::block_in_place passes a plain
    thread through and @tokio::runtime::Handle::current then panics for the absent runtime.
  Every such synchronous entry point panics when called in the async execution context of a
    current-thread runtime (or a LocalSet), on the locked tokio `1.52.3` build with the
    text `can call blocking only when running on the multi-threaded runtime`; nested
    @block_in_place within an outer blocking context — as on the tenant label path — succeeds
    on a multi-thread runtime.
  @get_client and @get_client_async panic with
    `cannot create the Kubernetes client: {e}` whenever @kube::Client::try_default fails —
    no kubeconfig resolvable and no in-cluster environment being the concrete production
    trigger.
  No function in this module has a typed error channel: the tenant-branch cluster read of
    @get_labels never surfaces its failure (flattened to `""`), and @wire_core_k8s,
    @init_k8s, @get_client_name, @get_short_name and @get_reporter never panic.

Handles:
  @VynilContext::None as both the initial state and after-context state — @get_owner_ns,
    @get_owner and @get_labels all return @None.
  Re-entrant setting — every @set_* replaces whatever variant was stored, so mixed-kind
    sequences simply end at the last write.
  Absent `metadata` name, namespace or uid fields — rendered as `""` in owner and label
    values, and @Some(`""`) from @get_owner_ns.
  @VynilContext::JukeBox — owner reference and jukebox-type labels are produced but
    @get_owner_ns stays @None.
  Missing, absent-label or failed tenant resolution on @VynilContext::TenantInstance — falls
    back respectively to the namespace value, published as the empty string.
  Unrecognized executable file names and @std::env::current_exe failure — generic
    `vynil.solidite.fr` client name and `vynil` short name.
  Unset `POD_NAME` — reporter instance `unknown`.
  Repeat or partial pre-registration of `vynil-core` hooks — silently ignored per hook by the
    core-side @OnceLock.

Tasks:
  [ ] Cover the three getters on the untouched @VynilContext::None default returning @None.
  [ ] Cover @set_* replacement semantics: second call overwrites the first, mixed-kind
      sequences end at the last write, no error on overwrite.
  [ ] Pin @get_owner key sets, kind strings, fixed `apiVersion`, `blockOwnerDeletion` and
      `controller` values for all four payload variants, including `""` for absent `name`/`uid`.
  [ ] Pin @get_labels key sets per variant: instance labels with `spec.package`/`spec.category`,
      the tenant-only `vynil.solidite.fr/tenant` key, and JukeBox with its three keys only.
  [ ] Cover the tenant label resolution: namespace label value, fallback to the namespace name
      when unlabeled, `""` on no-namespace or unreachable cluster, and the `TENANT_LABEL`
      key override.
  [ ] Cover @get_short_name for two-, three- and four-part client names (`vynil` vs the
      `{second}-{first}` form) and the @get_client_name `agent`/`operator`/other name mapping —
      testability bounded by the @std::env::current_exe dependency (see the `[?]` below).
  [ ] Cover @get_reporter with `POD_NAME` set and unset.
  [ ] Cover the panic surfaces: a sync accessor or setter called outside any runtime, one
      called under a current-thread runtime (e.g. `#[tokio::test(flavor = "current_thread")]`),
      and the @get_client/@get_client_async panic message with no resolvable configuration.
  [ ] Cover the wiring beyond @wire_core_k8s_populates_all_onelocks: assert a pre-registered
      or second @wire_core_k8s call keeps the first hook (first-wins), which today's single
      post-wire assertion does not pin.
  [ ] Cover @init_k8s inertness: observable context state identical across the call.
  [?] @CONTEXT is process-wide mutable global state with no reset or inspection surface: one
      test binary shares it across all tests and every module thread sees one slot. Decide
      later whether the global stays or a passed context object replaces it.
  [?] The sync-over-async wrappers (@block_in_place plus @Handle::block_on) make every sync
      entry panic outside a runtime or under a current-thread runtime, with the panic text
      coming from tokio and nothing documenting the precondition at the callsites. Decide
      later whether async-native accessors or an explicit precondition comment replaces this.
  [?] @get_client and @get_client_async panic instead of returning @crate::Result, and the
      message `cannot create the Kubernetes client: {e}` carries no stable unique error
      identifier as the project error rule asks. Decide later whether the suppliers become
      fallible and identified.
  [?] Both suppliers' doc comments call the result the "shared" client, yet each call rebuilds
      a full @kube::Client and re-reads kubeconfig or token files; only `vynil-core`'s lazy
      static reuses one injected instance. Decide later whether this module caches a client.
  [?] @init_k8s is an empty `const fn` dead stub that several call sites still invoke for no
      observable effect. Decide later whether it is removed or gains real initialization.
  [?] @get_owner_ns returns @Some(`""`) rather than @None for an instance with no namespace,
      so callers cannot distinguish "empty namespace" from "unknown". Decide later which
      polarity is intended.
  [?] The tenant branch of @get_labels flattens any resolution failure — no namespace, API
      down — into a published `vynil.solidite.fr/tenant: ""` label without a log, and holds
      the @CONTEXT read guard across that blocking cluster read, stalling concurrent setters.
      Decide later whether failures propagate or the read happens outside the lock.
  [?] @get_short_name shortens only names with more than three dot-parts, so the generic
      `vynil.solidite.fr` name never derives anything but `vynil`; whether the `> 3` guard is
      deliberate or off-by-one against three-part names is undetermined. Decide later.
  [?] Binary identity rides on @std::env::current_exe's file name: `operator` maps to the
      differently spelled `controller.vynil.solidite.fr` while every other shipped binary
      (diagnostic server, kubectl plugin) silently gets the generic `vynil.solidite.fr`
      field-manager and `User-Agent`. Decide later whether identity should come from build
      metadata or explicit configuration instead.
  [?] @get_client carries @must_use while its async twin @get_client_async does not. Decide
      later whether the asymmetry stays.
  [?] Because each core hook is OnceLock first-wins, a host that pre-registers any stub — a
      test harness, say — permanently shadows this module's closure for that hook while the
      remaining four still register, so a partially stubbed wiring is possible and silent.
      Decide later whether re-wiring must replace or refuse.

Done when:
  Every Scenario above has a passing mapped test, the coverage Tasks are closed or decided,
    and `cargo test -p common` is green.

Scenario: Fresh process starts with no context
  Given no @set_* has run
  When @get_owner_ns, @get_owner and @get_labels execute
  Then all three return @None
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Setters install and later setters replace the context
  Given a @TenantInstance installed through @set_tenant
  When @set_service runs afterwards with a @ServiceInstance
  Then all getters reflect the service instance only and the tenant value is gone
  And a second @set_tenant likewise replaces whatever was stored without error
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Owner reference shape per kind
  Given a @TenantInstance named `frontend` with `uid` `u-1`
  When @get_owner runs
  Then the object carries `apiVersion` `vynil.solidite.fr/v1`, `kind` `TenantInstance`,
    `name` `frontend`, `uid` `u-1`, `blockOwnerDeletion` `true` and `controller` `true`
  But a @VynilContext::JukeBox context yields the same keys with `kind` `JukeBox`
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Absent optional metadata yields empty strings
  Given an instance variant whose `metadata` lacks `name`, `namespace` and `uid`
  When @get_owner_ns, @get_owner and @get_labels run
  Then @get_owner_ns returns @Some of `""`
  And the owner `name`/`uid` values and label namespace field are all `""`
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: JukeBox context has an owner but no owner namespace
  Given a @VynilContext::JukeBox installed via @set_box
  When the three getters run
  Then @get_owner_ns returns @None
  But @get_owner returns the JukeBox-kind owner object and @get_labels the three-key jukebox
    label object
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Tenant label follows the namespace label
  Given a @TenantInstance in namespace `shops` labeled `vynil.solidite.fr/tenant: acme`
  When @get_labels runs
  Then `vynil.solidite.fr/tenant` is `acme`
  But when the namespace carries no tenant label the value falls back to `shops`
  And when the namespace has no namespace label source at all — the instance itself has no
    namespace — the value is `""` even though the rest of the labels are published
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Client names follow the running binary
  Given `agent` as the executable file name — then `operator` — then any other name — then an
    unresolvable path
  When @get_client_name and @get_short_name run
  Then the pairs are `agent.vynil.solidite.fr` with `vynil-agent`,
    `controller.vynil.solidite.fr` with `vynil-controller`, and `vynil.solidite.fr` with
    `vynil` for the last two cases
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Reporter carries the pod identity when present
  Given `POD_NAME` set to `vynil-agent-7f9b`
  When @get_reporter runs
  Then the reporter `instance` is `vynil-agent-7f9b` and `controller` is @get_short_name()
  But with `POD_NAME` unset the `instance` is `unknown`
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Unreachable cluster configuration panics out of both client suppliers
  Given no readable kubeconfig and no in-cluster environment
  When @get_client or @get_client_async runs
  Then the call panics with a message beginning `cannot create the Kubernetes client:`
    carrying the combined kubeconfig and in-cluster inference failure
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Sync context access require a multi-thread runtime
  Given @set_box or a getter invoked on a plain thread with no runtime
  When it runs
  Then it panics from @tokio::runtime::Handle::current before @CONTEXT is read or written
  But given the same call from inside a tokio multi-thread runtime task, it completes
  And given it from the async context of a current-thread runtime, @block_in_place panics
    with `can call blocking only when running on the multi-threaded runtime`
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Wiring registers the five injection hooks once
  Given a fresh process
  When @wire_core_k8s runs
  Then @vynil_core::k8s::context_is_wired reports true because all five @OnceLock hooks hold
    a closure
  Maps to test @wire_core_k8s_populates_all_onelocks
  The first-wins behaviour of a repeated or partially pre-registered call has no mapped test.

Scenario: init_k8s is inert
  Given any stored @VynilContext state
  When @init_k8s is called any number of times
  Then no observable state changes
  No mapped test exists.

Example:
  owner object for a tenant instance `frontend` with `uid` `u-1`: keys and values
    `apiVersion: "vynil.solidite.fr/v1"`, `kind: "TenantInstance"`, `name: "frontend"`,
    `uid: "u-1"`, `blockOwnerDeletion: true`, `controller: true`
  label object for that instance with `spec.package` `frontend`, `spec.category` `apps`,
    namespace `shops` labeled tenant `acme`: `app.kubernetes.io/managed-by: "vynil"`,
    `app.kubernetes.io/name: "frontend"`, `app.kubernetes.io/instance: "frontend"`,
    `vynil.solidite.fr/owner-namespace: "shops"`,
    `vynil.solidite.fr/owner-category: "apps"`,
    `vynil.solidite.fr/owner-type: "tenant"`,
    `vynil.solidite.fr/tenant: "acme"`
  reachable client names: `agent.vynil.solidite.fr`, `controller.vynil.solidite.fr`,
    `vynil.solidite.fr`; derived short names `vynil-agent`, `vynil-controller`, `vynil`
